<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10428"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 7:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Religion. Church attendance. Inner piety. Different entities entirely. Don&#39;t get them confused. They say that one cannot legislate morality. It is possible, however, to legislate morally conforming behaviors &#40;under threat of penalities&#41;, but one cannot legislate inner piety. Reputation is what men think of us, and character is what God and angels know of us. <BR> <BR>So goes the struggle between good and evil. The &#39;church&#39; person may have been the person that Rader wanted to be, and BTK was the result of his darkest self and a battle lost. <BR> <BR>He reminds me of a story I heard in which a young boy was trying to move a heavy object. He tried and used every imaginable tool and lever and could not move it. His father saw what he was doing and asked him if he had tried everything that he knew to do. The boy said &#39;yes&#39;. The father said &#39;No, you have not because you haven&#39;t asked me to help you&#39;. Rader was so self sufficient and proud that those two traits caused both his rise to infamy and his fall. <BR> <BR>I read that the minister said that he would be welcomed back to the church. Christians can be the worst for killing their wounded. Rader should have asked for help and he knew it. He is without excuse. I had a very Godly father, who by his every action, word, and deed pointed to a loving Heavenly Father. Because of my father&#39;s example, I am without excuse as well. <BR> <BR>Rader&#39;s entire life has been a devastating ruse. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
