</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 9:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If the Church that Rader is the PRESIDENT of doesn&#39;t watch out, they are in danger of being known as &#34;THE BTK CHURCH&#34;! <BR> <BR>Headed by a guy who is a known torturer &amp; killer of children &amp; helpless young mothers &amp; young ladies. Not only a disgusting piece of filth who has DONE these actions, but who is PROUD of having tortured &amp; killed an 11 year old girl by stripping her &amp; hanging her inside her parents basement. Then masturbating on her still-hanging semi-nude body. He has bragged about it &amp; taunted all the world about how he was proud of it &amp; had gotten away with it! <BR> <BR>Great use of judgement, REV. CLARK! Good thing that doesn&#39;t set off any &#39;red flags&#39; with the parishioners of the CHRIST LUTHERAN CHURCH that BTK is still PRESIDENT of! Wahoo! <BR> <BR>Wouldn&#39;t want to set a bad example for &#39;the kids&#39;, now, would we?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10437-->
<!--Post: 10483--><!--Time: 1109970514-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10483"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 1:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->PRESUMPTION OF INNOCENCE IN THE US IS DEAD. Thank you Victor et. al. who want Dennis Rader ostracized by everyone he knew even before we have been presented with a guilty verdict or confession. You are all proof that our system of justice is completely broken by media.  <BR> <BR>The smartest thing DR could do right now is plead innocent. Norman Williams and Nola Foulston are heading down a road to letting DTDC walk on technicalities anyway. <BR> <BR>Ron<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10483-->
<!--Post: 10506--><!--Time: 1109976606-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10506"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 2:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->RON: I agree that in the U.S. the media usually &#39;convicts&#39; the accused Before they go to trial. It&#39;s pretty unfair usually. But let&#39;s get real: <BR> <BR>1&#41; His DNA matched that which he left by masturbating on his torture-murder victims. <BR> <BR>2&#41; Good ol&#39; DENNY THE DOG CATCHER ACTUALLY CONFESSED to at least 6 torture-murders. Can&#39;t you see the writing on the wall? <BR> <BR>3&#41; No less than the Chief Of Police in Wichita stated plainly &#34;BTK is arrested!&#34; <BR> <BR>What part of &#34;BTK IS ARRESTED!&#34; do you Not understand?? <BR> <BR>I&#39;m sure his church knows he is the scumbag who did this too. So why keep such a despicable character in the position of PRESIDENT of his CHRIST LUTHERAN CHURCH? Give me a break.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10506-->
<!--Post: 10512--><!--Time: 1109979054-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10512"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 3:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Four scenarios: <BR> <BR>1- Reverend Clark announces that church President Dennis Rader has been suspended from this posision as president from the church while the investigation in BTK continues. If Rader is cleared or found innocent the church board will vote on his reinstatement. <BR> <BR>2- Reverend Clark reads a statement from Dennis Rader saying that due to the adverse publicity concerning his position as President of the church and for his concern over the members of the church congregation he will volunteraly step down from his position as president of the church until the investigation and or trail is concluded. <BR> <BR>3- Reverend Clark calls for a special meeting of the church&#39;s board of directors and they vote to permently remove Dennis Rader from his position as church president. <BR> <BR>4- Reverend Clark announces that Dennis Rader will remain in position as President of the church and Rader is relieved by this decision. <BR> <BR>Three of the four make sense to me.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10512-->
<!--Post: 10516--><!--Time: 1109980545-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10516"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 3:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->ok so which on is, is he still president or not, This should not even be an issue, who is in charge of this Denomination I want to write them a letter.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10516-->
<!--Post: 10527--><!--Time: 1109983005-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10527"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 4:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;EMBERSAGE&#34;: The above post by JOHNO was just a made up &#34;what if&#34; scenario which is not true. He was trying to jog our sense of morals. <BR> <BR>Yes, good ol&#39; Dennis Rader is STILL the PRESIDENT of Wichitas&#39; CHRIST LUTHERAN CHURCH! Good idea to write them a letter. Here is their web site: <a href="http://www.christ-lutheran.org/sermon/" target=_top>http://www.christ-lutheran.org/sermon/</a> <BR> <BR>Tho&#39; right now it doesn&#39;t show their street or Email addresses. Not to mention their phone number.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10527-->
<!--Post: 10536--><!--Time: 1109986802-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10536"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 5:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He was president of the congregation committee. It is like being in charge of refreshments, Bible school, parking, etc. It was just a committee. Church committees are a dime a dozen in all walks of life. He will be voted out and someone else will be voted to take that position.  Don&#39;t condemn the church members for his actions. They are in shock, along with his neighbors, coworkers, family, and probably an embarrassed WPD, who interviewed him as a possible suspect early in the investigation. He fit their profile. &#40;They should have trusted their profile, as it was obviously on target&#41;. As demonic as his acts were, the justice system still cloaks him in innocence until a jury decides otherwise. It will be very difficult to find uninformed or impartial jurors in that area. <BR> <BR>There but for the grace of God go we. All someone has to do is set you up like someone did Mr. V, and lo, everything hits the fan. The arrest, even if cleared, will follow you. You will never be free of the incident. It will forever appear on your criminal record. Potential employers may find out, etc. No one really believes that a person who got arrested is completely without fault. They had to have done something wrong to get in trouble in the first place. <BR>The case of the woman jogger viciously attacked in Central Park: What the hell was she doing out after dark to begin with?! She was asking for it, etc. Bad scene.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10536-->
<!--Post: 12389--><!--Time: 1112152442-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12389"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 29, 2005 - 7:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dennis Rader is apparently no longer the president of the church congregation council. Vice President Paul Shaw now serves in a dual position of Vice President and President Pro-Tem.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12389-->
